[env] _MOE_MM=True _MM_MAX_ROWS=100000 _SEG_BM=64
[build] production baseline mxfp8 8/32 ...
[build] affine 4/64 ...

============================================================================================
PREFILL rows: EXL3 vs PRODUCTION mxfp8 8-bit (the honest baseline)
============================================================================================
  rows  N=rows*k     EXL3 ms    mxfp8 ms     aff4 ms    ex/p8    ex/a4   gate1.7
   256      1536      52.533      26.110      20.839    2.012    2.521      MISS
   512      3072      54.152      35.576      29.329    1.522    1.846      PASS
  1024      6144      58.606      52.461      46.382    1.117    1.264      PASS
  2048     12288     112.322      86.073      81.232    1.305    1.383      PASS

If the segmented-GEMM path is disabled (EXL3_MOE_MM=0) the fallback tries
to materialize E*out*in*2 bytes and crashes on int32 overflow at E=128:
  128 * 5120 * 2304 * 2 = 3019898880 > INT32_MAX
  (E=384 -- the real V4.1 count -- would be 9.06 GB, so the fallback is
   never usable at full scale; the segmented path is mandatory.)
